{"chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01NJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0003": "$T$", "MATH_0004": "$s \\in \\Gamma(T, \\mathcal{L})$", "MATH_0005": "$T_s$", "MATH_0006": "$s$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{modules-lemma-s-open}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-apply}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-morphism-proj}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7b8444b4896c614c98ccd73b7ec0736007a81ce097e7aea5a3ff37895f0b9bd3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:72fd357d1a6b6542408d1e6bbe7045c1e7165d92bae91613c840ab964fabb1a8", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme and let <MATH_0002> be an invertible sheaf\non <MATH_0003>. For a section <MATH_0004> we denote\n<MATH_0005> the open subset of points where <MATH_0006> does not vanish. See\nModules, Lemma <REF_0001>. We can view the following\nlemma as a slight generalization of Lemma <REF_0002>.\nIt also is a generalization of Lemma <REF_0003>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0b18e5daa7b7119394914bae2a01eb07cf70083ddee92b711f77f3c5de6aadb9", "unit_id": "tag:01NJ:prose-0001"}
